  "description": "GONBUI crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C40 H50 Ce6 Mn4 N8 O44,2(C5 H5 N1),6(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Ce1 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce2 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce3 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn2 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Ce1B (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce2B (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce3B (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Mn1B (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn2B (Mn) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 26 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 2.809-4.382 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 94.24-149.34°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Ce6Mn4O12(O2CMe)10(NO3)4(py)4]·2py·6MeCN. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
